     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" data-account-id=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" accountid=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Andrew Woods</a> I am no longer able to replicated the problem \"SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input\" from the HTML UI by following the steps at <a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2055?focusedCommentId=50536&amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-50536\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2055?focusedCommentId=50536&amp;page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-50536</a> <br/>\n now. However, I am still able to replicate it with the copy I cloned earlier by Jun. 26th by stopping jetty, deleting the data in \"fcrepo4-data\" and restart jetty with \"mvn jetty:run -pl fcrepo-webapp\". It's something interesting! I think we can close the ticket now. What do you think?</p>",
